      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "13. Alas ! why do wise men live elsewhere, rejecting",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Kâs'i where the most rigorous penance (a life of entire absti-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "nence ) is (like) varied dinners given in gardens, where a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "strip of cloth to cover (the body ) is decent raiment, where",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the glory is an unlimited wandering for alms, and where",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "approaching death is like a blessing.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "14. Oh heart, leave those at whose gate (are heard) such",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "replies as “this is not the time for you ( to see the master ),”",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "“( he is ) now in private,” “ the master is asleep and “ if",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "you were to see him after waiting he would get angry”; and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "do you go to the temple of the Lord, the ruler of the world,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "which gives unbounded happiness, which is free from harsh-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ness, and where the cruel words of gatekeepers are not heard.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "15. May my days pass in some sacred forest, while mut-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tering the words “S'iva, S'iva, S'iva” with an eye regarding",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "equally a serpent or a wreath, a powerful enemy or a friend,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "a gem or a clod of earth, a bed of flowers or a stone, a blade",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of grass or a group of damsels.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
